[statement]
A mode field of two spaces, a NUL, zeros and a space, after another
member. Every reader reads mode 0. ferrotape refuses the archive: after
spaces and a NUL, Go reads the bytes that follow, and other digits there
are read apart.

[archive]
header name=first
data "1\n"
header name=odd mode="  \x000000 "
header name=after
end

[verdict]
all: refused HeaderField at 1024

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=- path=first size=2 mode=0o644 data="1\n"
member listed=- path=odd size=0 mode=0o0 data=""
member listed=- path=after size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
exit 0

